## 8. FINANCIAL CONTROL AND BUDGETING

The application must support three budgeting periods simultaneously:

### Daily Budget
- Daily spending limit.
- Remaining daily allowance.
- Daily spending summary.
- Warnings when the limit is approached or exceeded.

### Weekly Budget
- Weekly spending limits by category.
- Dedicated cigarette budget.
- Entertainment and hanging-out budget.
- Weekly obligations.
- Weekly financial evaluation.

### Monthly Budget
- Total monthly income.
- Total monthly expenses.
- Monthly category budgets.
- Savings progress.
- Debt repayment progress.
- Monthly financial evaluation.

The system must calculate the remaining available budget dynamically.

Do not calculate the daily budget simply by dividing the total monthly budget by 30.

The calculation must consider:
- Actual available money.
- Remaining days.
- Scheduled obligations.
- Essential expenses.
- Existing allocations.
- Income uncertainty.

