## 20. IMPORTANT SYSTEM RULES

The following rules are mandatory:

1. Never assume daily allowance income is guaranteed.
2. Record income only after it is actually received.
3. Separate freelance project money from personal money.
4. Deduct project operational expenses before distributing freelance profit.
5. Never count expected payments as available cash.
6. Never count account transfers as income or expenses.
7. Protect money reserved for essential expenses and obligations.
8. Do not treat savings as ordinary spending money.
9. Give discretionary expenses stricter budget controls.
10. Allow the cigarette spending limit to be configured manually.
11. Support daily, weekly, and monthly budgets simultaneously.
12. Automatically determine the financial mode using actual financial conditions.
13. Prioritize financial recovery before aggressive investing.
14. Distinguish essential expenses from discretionary spending.
15. Do not generate unrealistic financial predictions.
16. Do not impose arbitrary allocation percentages.
17. Make financial calculations transparent and explainable.
18. Keep transaction entry simple despite the application's comprehensive features.

